          "summary": "Authorizes Salem City to impose a sales and use tax of one-tenth of one percent (0.1%), one cent for every ten dollars spent on taxable purchases in the city, for ten years. The revenue would fund recreational (including parks) and cultural facilities and organizations, such as parks, trails, playing fields and courts, senior facilities, and arts and cultural programs.",
